        "raw": "<p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks for the thoughts! &nbsp;Yes, by Ranger I mean Chrono-Ranger. &nbsp;</p><p>Wraith seems to me something of a special case, as she can do so many things well. &nbsp;I think I could put Wraith in all the categories.</p><p>Absolute Zero can certainly be a damage dealer. &nbsp;The main feature as a new player, however, is to know he is completely dependant on his equipment. &nbsp;I could have called the category &quot;Equipment Dependant&quot;, but that didn&#39;t sound very heroic :)</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13.333333015441895px; line-height: 20px;\">Establishing categories is just food for thought and conversation. &nbsp;I really don&#39;t know if my chart is very useful for new players, but it&#39;s been fun to think about the characters and their roles. &nbsp;I love how each hero is so unique and yet still gets their job done.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think it would be cool to try playing a character in a functional role that they normally don&#39;t have. &nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13.333333015441895px;\">For example, how could you use Ra as a support character? &nbsp;Maybe send some fire damage over to a well equipped Absolute Zero? &nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13.333333015441895px;\">How would you use Ra as a tank? &nbsp;Maybe summon his staff, destroy it, and repeat? Maybe search for immunity to fire and manipulate hit points to become the target that gets hit by fire damage? &nbsp;</span></p><p>Playing a character &quot;against the grain&quot; might miss out on the main advantages, but could be fun and interesting. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Jason</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
